# What must never enter the image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so without this file the build context is the
# whole working directory. That shipped three categories of thing that must not
# be in a deployed image:
#
#   1. SECRETS. `.env` holds the real JWT signing key and the Google/Microsoft
#      client secrets. Anyone who can pull the image can read them, and they
#      survive in the layer even if a later step deletes the file.
#   2. ~420 MB of dead weight — dist/KredoAgent.exe (389 MB), the compressed
#      SQLite snapshot (28 MB) and the .sql backups (3.7 MB) — none of which the
#      running service opens.
#   3. Stale state: __pycache__ built against a different Python, plus logs and
#      uploads from the developer's machine landing on top of the runtime dirs.

# ---- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- Version control / tooling ----------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# ---- Local runtime state (the container makes its own; on Render the uploads
#      directory is a mounted disk, so a copy from the build context would be
#      shadowed by the mount anyway) ------------------------------------------
uploads/
logs/
*.log

# ---- Python build artefacts --------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ---- Databases, dumps and backups -------------------------------------------
*.db
*.db.gz
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.sql
backup_*.sql
*.db.backup_*
dump.rdb

# ---- The Windows agent build. 389 MB, runs on the user's own PC, and the
#      server has no use for it. --------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
KredoAgent.spec

# ---- Tests and developer scripts. The image runs the service; it does not run
#      the suite. Keep `fixtures/` out for the same reason. ------------------
tests/
fixtures/
scripts/
!scripts/db_migrate.py
docs/

# ---- ML training-time material. The runtime loads exactly one artefact,
#      mlmodel/artifacts/categorizer_model.joblib (app/categorization/
#      ml_service.py), so the training corpora, notebooks, HTML reports and
#      CatBoost logs are not needed. `mlmodel/artifacts/` is NOT excluded. ----
mlmodel/catboost_info/
mlmodel/artifacts_backup_*/
mlmodel/models_existing_eval/
mlmodel/models_newsheet_eval/
mlmodel/tests/
mlmodel/*.html
mlmodel/*.csv
mlmodel/*.pdf

# ---- Loose data files in the project root -----------------------------------
data.csv
data_combined.csv
data_original.csv
